            <ArticleTitle>Autologous patch angioplasty of the left main coronary artery in a pediatric patient: 7-year follow-up.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1457-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a patient who developed ischemia after an arterial switch procedure for transposition of the great vessels secondary to left coronary artery stenosis. The excellent intermediate-term result of patch angioplasty of the left main coronary artery with the use of an internal thoracic artery patch is outlined.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
